{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.OneDim.NoThreeCellOnTheChain","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.OneDim.NoThreeCellOnTheChain","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.LinearLayoutNoBulk","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.not_linearLayout_of_triangle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.not_linearLayout_of_triangle","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/NoThreeCellOnTheChain.lean#L78-L82","doc":"Contrapositive, in the form a consumer wants: a graph carrying three mutually adjacent sites\nis **not** a linear layout, so it is not a coordination graph the nuclear encoding can produce. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.OneDim.no_triangle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.OneDim.no_triangle","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/OneDim/NoThreeCellOnTheChain.lean#L66-L76","doc":"**A linear layout has no triangle.** Adjacency in a linear layout forces the two indices to be\nconsecutive, and three indices cannot be pairwise consecutive: if `a` and `b` differ by one and\n`b` and `c` differ by one, then `a` and `c` differ by zero or two, never by one.\n\nThis is the combinatorial content of \"the chain has no 3-cell\". ","signatureChunk":0}]}